---
title: Capture Payment Workflow — Sequence Diagram
---
sequenceDiagram
    actor Merchant
    participant AdminAPI as Admin API Route<br/>/admin/payments/:id/capture
    participant WF as capturePaymentWorkflow
    participant CapStep as capturePaymentStep
    participant PaySvc as PaymentModuleService
    participant ProvSvc as PaymentProviderService
    participant Provider as IPaymentProvider<br/>(e.g. Stripe)
    participant EventBus as Event Bus
    participant DB as PostgreSQL

    Merchant->>AdminAPI: POST /admin/payments/:id/capture { amount? }
    AdminAPI->>WF: workflow.run({ payment_id, amount })

    WF->>CapStep: capturePayment({ payment_id, amount })
    CapStep->>PaySvc: capturePayment({ payment_id, amount }, context)

    PaySvc->>DB: BEGIN
    PaySvc->>DB: SELECT Payment WHERE id = payment_id
    PaySvc->>DB: SELECT SUM(captures.amount) remaining

    alt amount > remaining capturable
        PaySvc->>DB: ROLLBACK
        PaySvc-->>CapStep: MedusaError INVALID_DATA
        CapStep-->>WF: throw
        WF-->>AdminAPI: 400 Bad Request
        AdminAPI-->>Merchant: Error response
    else amount is valid
        PaySvc->>ProvSvc: capturePayment(payment, amount)
        ProvSvc->>Provider: capturePayment({ data, amount })
        Provider-->>ProvSvc: { data: providerResult }

        ProvSvc-->>PaySvc: capture result

        PaySvc->>DB: INSERT Capture { payment_id, amount }
        PaySvc->>DB: UPDATE Payment.captured_at (if fully captured)
        PaySvc->>DB: UPDATE PaymentCollection.captured_amount = SUM(captures)
        PaySvc->>DB: UPDATE PaymentCollection.status (recalculate)
        PaySvc->>DB: COMMIT

        PaySvc->>EventBus: emit payment.captured (after commit)
        PaySvc-->>CapStep: PaymentDTO

        CapStep-->>WF: PaymentDTO
        WF-->>AdminAPI: { payment: PaymentDTO }
        AdminAPI-->>Merchant: 200 OK

        Note over PaySvc,DB: Compensation (if provider call succeeds<br/>but DB write fails):<br/>provider.refundPayment(captureData)
    end
